#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:13
msgid "Program Memory Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:15
msgid ""
"PlatformIO calculates firmware/program memory usage based on the next "
"segments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:0
msgid "``.text``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:19
msgid ""
"The code segment, also known as a text segment or simply as text, is where a "
"portion of an object file or the corresponding section of the program's "
"virtual address space that contains executable instructions is stored and is "
"generally read-only and fixed size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:0
msgid "``.data``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:26
msgid ""
"The .data segment contains any global or static variables which have a pre-"
"defined value and can be modified. The values for these variables are "
"initially stored within the read-only memory (typically within ``.text``) "
"and are copied into the ``.data`` segment during the start-up routine of the "
"program. Example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:0
msgid "``.bss``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:39
msgid ""
"Uninitialized data is usually adjacent to the data segment. The BSS segment "
"contains all global variables and static variables that are initialized to "
"zero or do not have explicit initialization in the source code. For "
"instance, a variable defined as ``static int i;`` would be contained in the "
"BSS segment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:45
msgid "The rough calculation could be done as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:47
msgid "PROGRAM (Flash) = ``.text`` + ``.data``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:48
msgid "DATA (RAM) = ``.bss`` + ``.data``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/program-memory-usage.rst:50
msgid ""
"If you need to print **all memory sections and addresses**, please use :"
"option:`pio run --verbose` command."
msgstr ""

